    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Camperdown-Campus/Education-Support-Lead_0157977-2": {
      "title": "Education Support Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nFull time, fixed term until October 2027    Exciting opportunity to be an Education Support Lead within the Faculty of Medicine and Health      Base Salary starting at $117,133 + 17% superannuation     About the opportunity   The Faculty of Medicine and Health is seeking an experienced and collaborative Education Support Lead to oversee the delivery of education support services and ensure the effective administration of learning and teaching activities.  Supporting a portfolio of academic programs, the role provides leadership to education support staff while maintaining a strong operational focus across curriculum administration, assessment, compliance, reporting and student support activities. Working closely with academic and professional staff, you will coordinate education processes, support continuous improvement initiatives and contribute to the delivery of a high-quality student experience.  This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced education professional who enjoys leading people, improving processes and building strong stakeholder relationships in a dynamic and complex environment.  Your key responsibilities will be to:   lead and coordinate the delivery of education support services across the work area, ensuring effective and consistent administrative support for learning and teaching activities  supervise and support education support staff, providing coaching, guidance and performance development  build and maintain productive relationships with academic, teaching and professional staff to support education priorities and operational requirements  provide advice and guidance on University policies, procedures and education administration processes  oversee teaching administration activities, including curriculum support, assessments, examinations, results processing, student evaluations, scholarships and student case management processes  coordinate program evaluation activities and support continuous improvement initiatives to enhance education delivery and student outcomes  manage education systems, records and reporting requirements, ensuring data accuracy, compliance and effective use of University platforms  oversee the development and maintenance of learning and teaching resources, including online learning environments such as Canvas  support the onboarding and training of academic and sessional teaching staff in relevant systems and education processes  coordinate the implementation of Faculty and University education projects and initiatives  review and analyse data to support operational planning, reporting and decision making  contribute to communities of practice and collaborative initiatives across Education Support teams  identify opportunities to improve processes, streamline service delivery and enhance the staff and student experience  undertake other duties and project work appropriate to the classification level.    About you   You are an experienced education professional with strong organisational and leadership skills, a commitment to service excellence and the ability to build effective working relationships across a complex environment. You thrive in roles that combine people leadership with hands on operational delivery and enjoy working collaboratively to achieve shared outcomes.  To be successful, you will have:  tertiary qualifications in a relevant discipline or an equivalent combination of training and experience  demonstrated experience in education administration, preferably within a higher education environment  experience leading or supervising staff and contributing to a positive, high performing team culture  experience supporting key education administration processes, including curriculum, assessment and student related activities  knowledge of university policies, procedures and administrative frameworks relevant to learning and teaching  experience using learning management systems and student administration systems, including platforms such as Canvas  highly developed communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively with a diverse range of staff  strong analytical, problem solving and decision making skills  excellent organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines  a commitment to continuous improvement and delivering high quality services.    Sponsorship / work rights for Australia   Work Rights: you must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment.    Pre-employment checks   Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University. Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment.  EEO statement    At the University of Sydney, our shared values include diversity and inclusion and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community which reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this commitment through our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTIQ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.   How to apply   Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.    For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply.  For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Ajaypal Singh, Recruitment Operations by email to ajaypal.singh@sydney.edu.au.  © The University of Sydney  The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment.    Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Wednesday 21 October 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Forest-Lodge/Senior-Business-Analyst_0154395-1": {
      "title": "Senior Business Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nFull time, fixed term maternity leave cover until 7th April 2028 Improve and optimize finance reporting and planning processes by capturing requirements Base Salary HEO8, $131,108 p.a.+ 17% superannuation       About the opportunity    The Senior Business Analyst will utilize technical and interpersonal skills to effectively engage with stakeholders to capture requirements and document existing and new processes. This position will support the lifecycle of the Financial Planning, Analytics & Commercial team’s reporting and planning projects by leading the tasks of requirements gathering, report wireframes, the writing and execution of testing scripts, rollout, and support.  The position will also be involved in AI projects around reporting key financial figures by writing User Stories, defining Personas and Journey paths. The position requires both an enthusiasm for change, an interest in Business Intelligence systems and experience in reporting and planning projects. Furthermore, this position is expected to assist in troubleshooting issues during the go live “hyper care” phase. As well as transitioning the support from project hyper care to standard BAU support.   Your key responsibilities will be to:   build effective relationships and work collaboratively with all staff in the Finance PSU and staff in other areas to identify and develop initiatives that optimise processes manage the development and implementation of test plans (System and UAT testing) to ensure dashboard/reporting or planning requirements have been delivered in line with the Business Intelligence strategy and timeframes lead workshops and meetings with project and stakeholder teams to identify, document and implement business improvements relating to Finance Business Intelligence and Planning and Budgeting processes collaborate with project managers to support the effective delivery of large Financial Services projects. For smaller internal team projects, develop project plans and track progress through to implementation drive the rollout and adoption of projects by developing and providing knowledge base content, user training and ongoing system education relating to BI or Planning modules.     About you   bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (Accounting degree preferred, or strong experience in Finance/Planning Reporting projects) membership of Institute of Chartered Accountants or Certified Practicing Accountants Australia preferred previous experience in financial planning and budgeting systems experience in Financial Reporting projects and systems ability to communicate effectively with analytical and problem-solving skills.     Sponsorship / work rights for Australia   You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to be eligible to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment.    Pre-employment checks and declarations      Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University.  Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment.     EEO statement     At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTQIA+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.    We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .    How to apply   Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.    For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply.   For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Kevin Lim, Recruitment Operations by email to Victoria.ford-rogers@sydney.edu.au .   © The University of Sydney   The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Sunday 25 October 2026 11:59 PM"
